	(text "Through-hole level shifters. There is no DIP version of the 74ALVC164245, so each direction is its own chip."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 10 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d021d6ab-17dd-40e8-8517-a2cf42f805d5")
	)
	(text "74AHCT245, supply 5 V: the FPGA side is the input (3.3 V is a valid high) and the S-100 side is the 5 V output. Direction is strapped A to B, pin 1 to 5 V. 74LVC245, supply 3.3 V: the S-100 side is the input (these inputs accept 5 V) and the FPGA side is the 3.3 V output. Direction is strapped B to A, pin 1 to 0 V. Pin 19, marked CE on the symbol, is the active-low output enable. LS_BUS_DIR and LS_DATA_DIR stay on the FPGA connector with pull-ups, and are not wired to a direction pin: reversing an AHCT245 would drive 5 V into the FPGA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b97a676a-5ed8-44a7-995a-93742e227dba")
	)
	(text "Every output enable is pulled up, so the transceivers stay off until the FPGA is configured. Exception: U10 is enabled all the time, and its inputs are pulled down so PHI and CLOCK stay low until then."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b8c6cca8-7749-40df-8eaa-39a7b2a5761c")
	)
