	(text "Open-collector translators: one 2N7000 per shared line, the through-hole stand-in for the BSS138. The gate is tied to 3.3 V. The FPGA side has 10 k to 3.3 V. The FPGA drives 0 or lets go."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "51c7d0ae-7c50-4411-8815-2d4134b5614e")
	)
	(text "A 2N7000 is specified to need up to 3.0 V between gate and source before it conducts. With the gate at 3.3 V that is a thin margin. Pick a device that actually switches at 3.3 V (measure gate threshold below about 2.5 V). The bus side has no pull-up of its own: the backplane terminator holds these lines at 2.7 V through 270 ohm. Pin 98 ERROR* and pin 99 POC* are not on that terminator, so only those two have 2.2 k to 5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12 228 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "726664e4-a005-4a7e-ad67-d061fdcc271c")
	)
